      "spam": false,
      "statusChangeID": null,
      "value": "Now that Rec Room is shutting down in about 9 days as of writing this, people may come to VRChat as an alternative. It might be a good time as ever to consider adding this feature. However, Rec Room does not have a requirement for their Voice Changer, so adding a requirement for it seems pointless considering PC users can use software like VoiceMod anyway to get around it.",
      "viewerReactions": null,
      "voteID": null
    }
  ],
  "companyID": "58c62e995865713647a7115d",
  "created": "2025-08-15T22:48:19.220Z",
  "deletedAt": null,
  "deletedBy": null,
  "details": "It's widely known that Quest users are unable to access voice changer applications, and some PC users may find these processes too complex. I would like to suggest a feature built into VRChat with settings to adjust pitch, reverb, modulation, etc. This could also include the ability to save these changes to one of 5 - 10 'voice profiles', allowing users to swap between different voice changer settings easily. \n\nI understand that this could be a feature utilised by bad actors, hence there are 4 methods I have devised to help combat these people from posing as a younger person to decieve the younger audience:\n\n1. Require 18+ ID verification \n\n2. Require a certain trust level (likely Known / Trusted)\n\n3. Exclusive to VRChat+\n\n4. Combination of all the above!\n\nThe 4th option may be slightly overkill, but it would be the best choice to maximise user safety. The feature would help immensely for role-playing, performing, and voice acting without restricting it from Quest users.",
